Are you an organized and motivated Architectural Project Manager/Architect with 8+ years of experience looking to join a highly collaborative and creative workplace? We have an exciting opportunity waiting for you!

MKSD is seeking forward-thinking problem solvers who can lead and manage a variety of architectural projects to join our team!

A critical part of MKSD’s success is our talented staff members who believe in and live out the MKSD core values: perseverance, selflessness, passion, forward thinking, honesty and progressive thinking.

As a team, we have built a creative culture where everyone is valued, included and empowered. Our values are translated to each client and imbedded in our projects with the purpose of enhancing life. Our practice creates meaningful projects, from transformative renovations to highly complex buildings. Each project’s solution is tailored to the individual needs of our clients and encompasses all phases of planning, design and construction.

Our ideal candidate would share in our passion and is highly motivated, skilled and committed with a positive attitude! Our team currently has an opening for the following positions:

Project Manager l Architect – MKSD is seeking a talented and hardworking Project Manager/Architect to join our team. PM/RA shall be a registered architect. Candidates should have a college degree in the field of Architecture (BArch or MArch) or a related building design discipline and 8-15 years of working experience.

As a Project Manager at MKSD, you will enjoy opportunities for innovation, design, client interaction, and direct collaboration with project team members from architectural and other engineering disciplines. Responsibilities include:

Team leadership, and overseeing the production and coordination of several projects concurrently;
Conducting schematic design, design development and contract document work sessions in conjunction with clients, project staff, and representatives from other disciplines;
Preparing technical drawings and specifications to ensure that our projects conform to specifications, codes, standards, and client requirements;
Coordinating with both architecture and engineering team members to deliver an integrated set of documents across all contracted disciplines;
Working with BIM model for integration and coordination of building systems and distribution;
Establishing good client relationships and coordinating with outside consultants;
Participating in marketing, contractual, design and production meetings;
Coordinating with the Partner in Charge for project reviews; and
Acting as a mentor for less experienced Project Designers.

Je hebt minimum 5 jaar werfervaring;

Je volgt het project op in de uitvoeringsfase met oog voor planning, budget en kwaliteit;

Je stuurt de aanbestedingsdossiers bij en geeft feedback aan de ontwerpers;

Je hebt technische kennis van kantoor- en industriegebouwen;

Je kent de flow van vergunningen en wettelijke verplichtingen van een bouwproject;

BIM minded zijn, MS 365 is gekend en digitale tools gebruiken op de werf.

Je waakt over de voortgang, risico’s en beslissingsmomenten binnen het project;

Je zorgt voor een correcte verslaggeving van de werf en opleveringen.

Proactief communiceren met alle betrokken partijen.

